*> The spawn info of the hand-written bytes: type 5, "a:b", seed 1, mode 2, previous none, debug,
*> no flat, no death location, cooldown 3, sea level 63.
 SPAWN-DEFAULTS.
     INITIALIZE PB-SPAWN-INFO
     MOVE 5 TO PB-SI-DIM-TYPE
     MOVE 3 TO PB-SI-DIM-LENGTH
     MOVE "a:b" TO PB-SI-DIM
     MOVE 1 TO PB-SI-SEED
     MOVE 2 TO PB-SI-GAME-MODE
     MOVE -1 TO PB-SI-PREVIOUS-MODE
     MOVE 1 TO PB-SI-DEBUG
     MOVE 3 TO PB-SI-PORTAL-COOLDOWN
     MOVE 63 TO PB-SI-SEA-LEVEL.

 LOGIN-DEFAULTS.
     INITIALIZE PB-LOGIN
     MOVE 1 TO PB-LG-ENTITY
     MOVE 2 TO PB-LG-DIM-COUNT
     MOVE 3 TO PB-LG-DIM-LENGTH(1)
     MOVE "a:b" TO PB-LG-DIM-NAME(1)
     MOVE 3 TO PB-LG-DIM-LENGTH(2)
     MOVE "c:d" TO PB-LG-DIM-NAME(2)
     MOVE 20 TO PB-LG-MAX-PLAYERS
     MOVE 10 TO PB-LG-VIEW-DISTANCE
     MOVE 10 TO PB-LG-SIM-DISTANCE
     MOVE 1 TO PB-LG-DEATH-SCREEN
     PERFORM SPAWN-DEFAULTS.

 PUT-SPAWN-BAD.
     CALL "PB-PUT-SPAWN-INFO" USING PB-BUFFER PB-SPAWN-INFO
     MOVE "ERROR" TO TL-EXPECTED.

 PUT-LOGIN-BAD.
     CALL "PB-PUT-LOGIN" USING PB-BUFFER PB-LOGIN PB-SPAWN-INFO
     MOVE "ERROR" TO TL-EXPECTED.

*> The spawn info as " <type> <dim> <seed> <mode> <previous> <debug> <flat> <present> <death dim> x y z
*> <cooldown> <sea>"; a failed read leaves all of it 0.
 SHOW-SPAWN.
     PERFORM START-OBS
     MOVE PB-SI-DIM-TYPE TO WS-EDIT
     PERFORM ADD-NUM
     IF PB-SI-DIM-LENGTH > 0
         STRING " " PB-SI-DIM(1:PB-SI-DIM-LENGTH) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
             WITH POINTER WS-PTR
     ELSE
         MOVE PB-SI-DIM-LENGTH TO WS-EDIT
         PERFORM ADD-NUM
     END-IF
     MOVE PB-SI-SEED TO WS-EDIT
     PERFORM ADD-NUM
     MOVE PB-SI-GAME-MODE TO WS-EDIT
     PERFORM ADD-NUM
     MOVE PB-SI-PREVIOUS-MODE TO WS-EDIT
     PERFORM ADD-NUM
     MOVE PB-SI-DEBUG TO WS-EDIT
     PERFORM ADD-NUM
     MOVE PB-SI-FLAT TO WS-EDIT
     PERFORM ADD-NUM
     MOVE PB-SI-DEATH-PRESENT TO WS-EDIT
     PERFORM ADD-NUM
     IF PB-SI-DEATH-LENGTH > 0
         STRING " " PB-SI-DEATH-DIM(1:PB-SI-DEATH-LENGTH) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
             WITH POINTER WS-PTR
     ELSE
         MOVE PB-SI-DEATH-LENGTH TO WS-EDIT
         PERFORM ADD-NUM
     END-IF
     MOVE PB-SI-DEATH-X TO WS-EDIT
     PERFORM ADD-NUM
     MOVE PB-SI-DEATH-Y TO WS-EDIT
     PERFORM ADD-NUM
     MOVE PB-SI-DEATH-Z TO WS-EDIT
     PERFORM ADD-NUM
     MOVE PB-SI-PORTAL-COOLDOWN TO WS-EDIT
     PERFORM ADD-NUM
     MOVE PB-SI-SEA-LEVEL TO WS-EDIT
     PERFORM ADD-NUM.

*> Login: entity, hardcore, dimension count and names, max players, view, simulation, reduced
*> debug, death screen, limited crafting, online mode, secure chat.
 SHOW-LOGIN.
     PERFORM START-OBS
     MOVE PB-LG-ENTITY TO WS-EDIT
     PERFORM ADD-NUM
     MOVE PB-LG-HARDCORE TO WS-EDIT
     PERFORM ADD-NUM
     MOVE PB-LG-DIM-COUNT TO WS-EDIT
     PERFORM ADD-NUM
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > PB-LG-DIM-COUNT
         STRING " " PB-LG-DIM-NAME(WS-I)(1:PB-LG-DIM-LENGTH(WS-I)) DELIMITED BY SIZE
             INTO TL-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-PTR
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE PB-LG-MAX-PLAYERS TO WS-EDIT
     PERFORM ADD-NUM
     MOVE PB-LG-VIEW-DISTANCE TO WS-EDIT
     PERFORM ADD-NUM
     MOVE PB-LG-SIM-DISTANCE TO WS-EDIT
     PERFORM ADD-NUM
     MOVE PB-LG-REDUCED-DEBUG TO WS-EDIT
     PERFORM ADD-NUM
     MOVE PB-LG-DEATH-SCREEN TO WS-EDIT
     PERFORM ADD-NUM
     MOVE PB-LG-LIMITED-CRAFT TO WS-EDIT
     PERFORM ADD-NUM
     MOVE PB-LG-ONLINE-MODE TO WS-EDIT
     PERFORM ADD-NUM
     MOVE PB-LG-SECURE-CHAT TO WS-EDIT
     PERFORM ADD-NUM.

*> The sum of every Login field and the spawn info: 0 after a failed read.
 SHOW-LOGIN-ZERO.
     PERFORM START-OBS
     COMPUTE WS-EDIT = PB-LG-ENTITY + PB-LG-HARDCORE + PB-LG-DIM-COUNT + PB-LG-DIM-LENGTH(1)
         + PB-LG-MAX-PLAYERS + PB-LG-VIEW-DISTANCE + PB-LG-SIM-DISTANCE + PB-LG-REDUCED-DEBUG
         + PB-LG-DEATH-SCREEN + PB-LG-LIMITED-CRAFT + PB-LG-ONLINE-MODE + PB-LG-SECURE-CHAT
         + PB-SI-DIM-TYPE + PB-SI-DIM-LENGTH + PB-SI-SEED + PB-SI-GAME-MODE + PB-SI-SEA-LEVEL
     PERFORM ADD-NUM.

 FILL.
     CALL "TEST-FILL-HEX" USING WS-HEX PB-BUFFER.

*> Removes the spaces of WS-HEX (a short hex string of a few dozen bytes).
 HEX-COMPACT.
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-HEX-A
     MOVE 1 TO WS-PTR
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 1024
         IF WS-HEX(WS-I:1) NOT = SPACE
             MOVE WS-HEX(WS-I:1) TO WS-HEX-A(WS-PTR:1)
             ADD 1 TO WS-PTR
         END-IF
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE WS-HEX-A TO WS-HEX.

*> WS-NBT and WS-NBT-LEN from the hex bytes of WS-HEX.
 NBT-FROM-HEX.
     CALL "TEST-FILL-HEX" USING WS-HEX PK-BUFFER
     MOVE LOW-VALUES TO WS-NBT
     MOVE PK-LENGTH TO WS-NBT-LEN
     CALL "PB-GET-BYTES" USING PK-BUFFER WS-NBT WS-NBT-LEN.

*> WS-DATA from the hex bytes of WS-HEX.
 DATA-FROM-HEX.
     CALL "TEST-FILL-HEX" USING WS-HEX PK-BUFFER
     MOVE LOW-VALUES TO WS-DATA
     CALL "PB-GET-BYTES" USING PK-BUFFER WS-DATA PK-LENGTH.

*> Asserts the buffer of a writer: TL-EXPECTED is its hex, or "ERROR" when the write must fail,
*> which leaves nothing behind. The buffer is reset for the next case.
 CHECK-PUT.
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     CALL "TEST-BUFFER-HEX" USING PB-BUFFER TL-OBSERVED
     IF PB-ERROR = 1
         IF PB-LENGTH = 0
             MOVE "ERROR" TO TL-OBSERVED
         ELSE
             MOVE "ERROR-APPENDED" TO TL-OBSERVED
         END-IF
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED.

 START-OBS.
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE 1 TO WS-PTR.

 ADD-NUM.
     IF WS-PTR > 1
         STRING " " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-PTR
     END-IF
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-PTR.

 ADD-FLT.
     STRING " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-FLT) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-PTR.

*> Ends a read check: the observed fields, then " ok" or " e<error> p<position>" (ok means no
*> error and every byte read). TL-EXPECTED holds the expected text; START-OBS cleared it, so the
*> caller sets it after the fields and before this paragraph.
 END-GET.
     IF PB-ERROR = 0 AND PB-POS = PB-LENGTH
         STRING " ok" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-PTR
     ELSE
         MOVE PB-ERROR TO WS-EDIT
         STRING " e" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-PTR
         MOVE PB-POS TO WS-EDIT
         STRING " p" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-PTR
     END-IF
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED.
 END PROGRAM TEST-LEVEL-EVENTS.
 COPY PROTOTEST.
